Well, I finally did it - I installed Slash'em, and after lots of
deaths, I managed to super-lotsa-added-stuff overprepare!

I played W, the Vampire Wizard, and managed to get him through the
early game.  Vampires are awesome...but food and nutrition is really
an issue!  The only way I made it through the early game was prayer -
lots and lots of prayer!  You can't play slow and putz around; you
can't take lots of time to credit clone, you've got to worry about
food...early game, anyway.

Midgame, things got easier - bigger monsters show up, and bigger
monsters give you more nutrition (especially when you put them to
sleep and just eat them :p)  There were lots of altars in the game (3
_s in the teens alone), so I set up base camp near the Lawful quest,
and worked from there.  I also stumbled upon a medical kit, and they
are expensive, so I got a good start with credit cloning - I had free
ID services really close to my stash!

The real midgame excitement was clearing Ft Ludios.  I'd gotten the
Amulet of Misspelling early (only level 12 to go on the quest -
sweet!) so I had lots of power for spells, and had a few nice pets
(charm monster FTW!) and Magic Missile, plus some speed boots I'd
found, so I was ready to go!  I warped in with the Amulet, and I have
to recommend this as a decent strategy: you avoid the press at the
door!  Since soldiers are kind of slow, you can just keep running from
them while they blow themselves to bits with giant explosions (I later
read that bullets help explosions, too - a few dead soldiers and
BOOOM)  It was fun :)

I took out Sam with some boulders - 1st time I'd ever done that
trick.  I used Thiefbane occationally, but never had skillpoints to
get to basic until very late game.

Late game, I used every dirty trick I knew, except pudding farming.
OTOH, I had the Amulet of Endless Pw and Create Monster at 0%....so I
got the Wallet of Perseus, in addition to a naked AC of something like
-8.  I polymorphed rings and scrolls and ate so many until I got
teleport control and protection from shape changers, and tried for
increase attack...and then polymorphed to a cube to get poly control,
just for the heck of it (never used it again).  I also realized the
power of polymorphing scrolls - even in SLASH'EM.  A stack of 3
scrolls of genocide?  SWEET!  A stack of 3 scrolls of charging?  I
have to use them now; they'll revert back...hmmm....what to charge?
Added fun, I found a random /oWishing...and used something like 1 wish
from it midgame.  Between thrones, 2 /oWishing, and gypsies, I used 7
wishes and had ready 10 more wand uses, plus 3 magic lamps...did I
mention overprepared?  Plus just lucky.

I also discovered the flip side of Vampire nutrition.  You eat
*everything* you fight.  So I ended up with the problem that I was
overfull ALL THE TIME.  I eventually uncursed a = of Hunger and that
helped a bit.  Still, it was a serious problem - vomiting in the
middle of combat isn't cool.  I never could eat a Black D corpse for
the resistance.

Also on the overprepared theme:  when you've got 6 scrolls of
genocide, and nothing left worth blowing away, nurse dancing can get
over the top.  Add alchemy to those hitpoints.  Now add hitpoints from
drinking vampire blood (did I mention I threw up a lot from over
stuffing myself?).  I had over 900 hp!  And ~450 Pw!  It was crazy.

The run was a breeze.  I had been so worried after my earlier deaths
that I was ready for pretty much anything.  And then I met a Solar on
the plane of Fire.  Wow.  So, yeah, !oFullHealing only heal 500hp.
You don't get to see that in action much.  I never did see what killed
the thing; it just disappeared - maybe it got stoned as I had conflict
and it was stunned from Magicbane, but I never did find a statue.
Made me wary of Astral.

But...no Solars on Astral!  Took me 3 tries to find the right altar,
but I was okay with that.  Famine was a joke - I was hoping to get
unsatiated from him....never happened.  Pestilence?  No, I learned
Cure Disease early on and it was still good.  Death?  Magic Missile.

And all those angels and priests?  Man, do I love fireball!

So the moral is, if you break every conduct (except artifact wishing,
as Slash'em creates so many of the stupid things), it is possible to
win Slash'em!

My only complaint with Slash'em is the lack of encyclopedia entries
for the added monsters!  Ok, there's some blue demon here with some
weird name I've never seen before...WTF, it puts me to sleep?  What
*is* this thing?  I'm clearly going to have to do some research and
add some patches, eh?

Hack on,

